  <p class="app-title">Appendix V</p>
  <p class="app-subtitle">University Residences and Housing</p>

  {% if is_ba %}
  {# ── BA (UG) Housing — On-campus / University housing ── #}
  <p class="para">As part of its campus redevelopment plan, NLSIU is currently in the process of expanding its infrastructure and accommodation facilities. University Housing is, thus, temporarily limited. The University student accommodation plan entails that the university will endeavour to accommodate all incoming undergraduate students either in on-campus or off-campus university residences.</p>

  <p class="para">All students residing in the University Housing will be provided with the university's food plan at no additional charge. The food plan includes breakfast, lunch, evening snacks, and dinner. In case an off-campus residence is provided, the University will provide transportation facilities by bus (limited trips and timings).</p>

  <p class="para"><strong>Application</strong></p>

  <p class="para">If you wish to apply for University residence, you may indicate this preference in the application portal. The full housing fee of Rs. {{ housing_fee }}/- will then be included in your fee invoice and will have to be paid before {{ full_fee_deadline }}. Please note that applying for University residence does not guarantee allotment in particular residential facilities. Allocation will be made only at the time of admission and will depend on availability at that stage.</p>

  {% else %}
  {# ── LLB / MPP (PG) Housing — Off-campus (Olive / FF21) ── #}
  <p class="para">As part of its campus redevelopment plan, NLSIU is currently in the process of expanding its infrastructure and accommodation facilities. University housing is, thus, temporarily limited. The University student accommodation plan entails accommodating some incoming students from the postgraduate programmes in off-campus residences. Accordingly, the university has tied up with two reputed housing service providers – Olive Living and FF21, to provide accommodation to students outside the campus.</p>

  <p class="para">Olive @ RR Nagar is a venture of the Embassy group. It is located close to Nagarbhavi at RR Nagar – 5.3km (12 min) from the campus. RR Nagar is a vibrant locality in the vicinity of the university. Olive residence provides contemporary, fully equipped student residences with the following facilities. The residences have furnished rooms with attached modern bathrooms, 24-hour security, regular housekeeping, hi-speed Wi-Fi, a vending machine, common appliances such as a washing machine, fridge, induction stove and microwave, and a terrace common room with TV/entertainment facilities, dining space and sufficient seating.</p>

  <p class="para">"FF21@ RR Nagar" is a newly constructed and furnished co-living facility with twin-sharing rooms and attached washroom facilities. RR Nagar is a vibrant locality in the vicinity of the university. The rooms in FF21 are furnished and include attached modern bathrooms, 24-hour security, regular housekeeping and hi-speed Wi-Fi, with common facilities such as washing machines, fully functional pantry zones on each floor equipped with a fridge, induction stove, electric kettle, microwave and basic utensils, along with shared amenities including a lounge, mini movie screening theatre, pool table, table tennis, carrom, indoor games, cafeteria, two-wheeler parking and dining facilities.</p>

  <p class="para">The university is also exploring the possibility of adding similar such facilities as university residences for the academic year 2026-27. You may be allocated these new facilities.</p>

  <p class="para">All housing is allocated to a single occupant on a double-sharing basis. All students residing in the Off-Campus Housing will be provided with the university's food plan at no additional charge. The food plan includes breakfast, lunch, evening snacks, and dinner. The University provides transportation facilities by bus (limited trips and timings) from the off-campus facilities to the NLSIU campus.</p>

  <p class="para"><strong>Application</strong></p>

  <p class="para">If you wish to apply for University residence, you may indicate this preference in the application portal. The full off-campus housing fee of Rs. {{ housing_fee }}/- will then be included in your fee invoice and will have to be paid before {{ full_fee_deadline }}.</p>

  <p class="para">Please note that applying for University residence and paying the accommodation fees, does not guarantee allotment. While the University endeavours to expand its residential capacity, it is unable to guarantee housing at this time. Allocation will be made only at the time of registration and will depend on availability at that stage. If a student is not allotted University residence, the off campus housing fee paid will be refunded. However, a student who has been allotted university residences will not be refunded the amount in case of withdrawal, since the amount goes to a third-party service provider.</p>

  {% endif %}

  <p class="para"><strong>Other Housing Options</strong></p>

  <p class="para">NLSIU is located in Nagarbhavi, a well-connected part of Bengaluru with several residential localities nearby. Students usually have access to a range of private accommodation options, including hostels, paying guest facilities, and rental housing in and around Nagarbhavi, Chandra Layout, Vijayanagar, Rajarajeshwarinagar, Mallathahalli, Jnanabharathi, Nayandahalli, and Mysore Road. {% if is_pg %}Several current NLSIU students live in these localities. {% endif %}Students may independently explore these options based on their requirements, budget, and convenience.</p>

