  {# SECTION A — Provisional offer           #}
  {# ════════════════════════════════════════ #}
  <p class="faq-section-title">A. Provisional offer, acceptance and portal</p>

  <p class="faq-q">1. What does a "provisional" offer of admission mean?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">It means that NLSIU is offering you admission subject to completion of all admission formalities. Your admission becomes final only after you accept the offer, pay the required fees within the deadlines, submit all required documents and forms, and successfully complete in-person verification of original documents at NLSIU.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">2. How do I accept the provisional offer?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">See Appendix I of the Provisional Offer of Admission.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">3. What is the confirmation fee and when must it be paid?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">You must pay Rs. {{ confirmation_fee_amt }} as the confirmation fee by {{ confirmation_deadline }}. Failure to pay the confirmation fee by the deadline will result in withdrawal of the admission offer.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">4. Can I get the extension to pay the confirmation fees?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. No extension will be granted for payment of confirmation fees.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">5. Is the confirmation fee adjusted against the total fee payable?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. After the confirmation fee is paid, NLSIU will generate a balance fee invoice. You will then be required to log back into the portal and pay the remaining amount by the full-fee deadline.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">6. What if I do not want to accept the seat? What if I want to withdraw from the admission process?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Email nlsat.query@nls.ac.in from your registered email address. Your email should mention your full name, NLSAT application number, the programme offered, and a clear statement that you wish to withdraw your application. The date on which NLSIU receives the email will be used for refund calculations, wherever applicable. Once processed, the withdrawal is final.</p>

  {# ════════════════════════════════════════ #}
  {# SECTION B — Fees                        #}
  {# ════════════════════════════════════════ #}
  <p class="faq-section-title">B. Fees, fee payment and refund issues</p>

  <p class="faq-q">7. What is the deadline for full fee payment?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">The full fee payable by the candidate must be paid by 11:59 p.m. on {{ full_fee_deadline }}. This includes the balance amount after adjustment of the Rs. {{ confirmation_fee_amt }} confirmation fee.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">8. Can I pay the fee in installments?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. The full amount reflected in the fee invoice must be paid by the deadline unless NLSIU specifically communicates otherwise in writing.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">9. How is my fee amount calculated?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Your fee invoice will depend on your category, applicable refundable deposit, and whether you choose to apply for University {% if is_ba %}accommodation{% else %}off-campus accommodation{% endif %}. Candidates who apply for University residence will have the annual {% if is_ba %}housing{% else %}off-campus housing{% endif %} fee added to their invoice.</p>
  <p class="faq-a">If {% if is_ba %}housing{% else %}off-campus housing{% endif %} is included, the first-year amount payable is Rs. {{ total_scst_y1 }} for SC/ST candidates and Rs. {{ total_gen_y1 }} for General and other category candidates. This includes the one-time admission fee, annual tuition and facilities fee, annual {% if is_ba %}housing{% else %}off-campus housing{% endif %} fee, and the applicable refundable deposit.</p>
  <p class="faq-a">If the {% if is_ba %}housing{% else %}off-campus housing{% endif %} fee is not included, the first-year amount is expected to be the one-time admission fee, annual tuition and facilities fee, and the applicable refundable deposit. On the current fee schedule, this works out to Rs. {{ no_housing_scst }} for SC/ST candidates and Rs. {{ no_housing_gen }} for General and other category candidates. Candidates should rely on the fee invoice generated in the portal as the final amount payable.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">10. What does the {% if is_ba %}housing{% else %}off-campus housing{% endif %} fee include?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">The annual {% if is_ba %}housing{% else %}off-campus housing{% endif %} fee is Rs. {{ housing_fee }}. It includes the University food plan covering breakfast, lunch, evening snack and dinner. It is payable only where the candidate applies for University residence and the fee is included in the invoice.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">11. If I apply for University residence but am not allotted accommodation, will I get a refund?</p>
  {% if is_ba %}
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. Applying for University residence does not guarantee allotment. If you pay the housing fee but are not allotted University residence, the housing fee paid will be refunded.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. Applying for University residence does not guarantee allotment. If you pay the off-campus housing fee but are not allotted University residence, the off-campus housing fee paid will be refunded. However, a student who has been allotted university residences will not be refunded the amount in case of withdrawal, since the amount goes to a third-party service provider.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="faq-q">12. What happens if I miss the full-fee deadline?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Failure to pay the full fee by the deadline will result in withdrawal of the provisional offer and the candidate may not be registered as a student. If you face a payment issue, contact nlsat.query@nls.ac.in immediately with proof of the issue.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">13. Can I get the extension to pay the full fees?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No extensions will ordinarily be granted for payment of the full fees beyond the notified deadline. Candidates who are unable to make payment by the deadline, due to circumstances beyond their control, may submit a formal request for extension to nlsat.query@nls.ac.in. Any request for consideration on this basis must demonstrate the candidate's bona fides, including that the candidate had undertaken all reasonable efforts to complete the payment within the stipulated timeline, including applying under the PM VidyaLakshmi Scheme and education loans well on time, but was prevented from doing so due to circumstances beyond their control. The request must clearly set out the reasons for the delay, include supporting documents evidencing the circumstances relied upon, and specify the expected date of payment. The Registrar shall consider the request and determine whether any extension may be granted, and if so, the duration of such extension.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">14. What if my payment is debited but not reflected in the portal?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Take screenshots of the transaction, payment reference number, bank debit entry, and portal status. Write immediately to nlsat.query@nls.ac.in from your registered email address. Do not make repeated payments unless instructed or unless the payment gateway clearly fails and reverses the transaction.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">15. Can I get a fees certificate/ particular documents from the university for the sanction of an educational loan?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. Banks and financial institutions usually sanction loans based on the offer letter and the fee schedule. However, in case further documentation is required, you may apply to the university with an email to nlsat.finance@nls.ac.in with a copy to nlsat.query@nls.ac.in. The university can take up to 3-5 working days to issue documentation, so candidates are advised to apply well in advance of the fees deadline.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">16. What is the withdrawal and refund process?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">If you wish to withdraw, email nlsat.query@nls.ac.in from your registered email address with your full name, NLSAT application number, programme offered, and a clear withdrawal statement. The date NLSIU receives your email will count for refund calculations. Refunds, if any, will be governed by the applicable University refund rules and the withdrawal, once processed, is final.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">17. How much refund will I get if I withdraw from the process after {{ full_fee_day }} June?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Fees Refunds are governed by the applicable UGC and university regulations. The UGC has not yet notified regulations for fee refunds for the current academic year. The regulations will be updated on the university portal once they are notified.</p>

  {# ════════════════════════════════════════ #}
  {# SECTION C — Financial aid               #}
  {# ════════════════════════════════════════ #}
  <p class="faq-section-title">C. Financial aid, education loans and scholarships</p>

  <p class="faq-q">18. Can I apply for financial aid?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Candidates whose gross family income is less than Rs. 8,00,000 per annum are eligible to apply for University financial aid. The definition of 'family income' is the average gross family income for the last three financial years or the gross family income for the latest financial year, whichever is greater. For the determination of family income, family is considered as members of a family residing together which includes self, parents, sibling, spouse / partner of the student.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">19. Do I necessarily need to apply for PM Vidyalaxmi before applying for University financial aid?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. Before submitting a University financial-aid application, candidates must apply through the official PM Vidyalaxmi portal at https://pmvidyalaxmi.co.in and submit a copy or proof of the education-loan application along with the University financial-aid application. This is a pre-condition for the University financial-aid process.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">20. Does applying for financial aid exempt me from paying the full fee by {{ full_fee_deadline }}?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. For NLSAT admissions, applying for financial aid does not exempt you from paying the full fee by the deadline. Candidates must pay the full fee by {{ full_fee_deadline }}. If University financial aid is approved later, the fee will be reimbursed up to the extent of aid granted.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">21. When will I know the outcome of my financial-aid application?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">NLSIU will communicate decisions on financial-aid applications on or before 31 July 2026.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">22. If I do not have my parents' income-tax returns, can I still apply for financial aid?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. Where income-tax returns are not available, you may submit income certificates issued by government authorities, bank statements, and any other documents supporting the income earned by the family. The Financial Aid Committee may ask for further clarifications or documents.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">23. Can I apply for other scholarships?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. Admitted students may be eligible for scholarships sponsored by central and state governments and private organisations. NLSIU has curated a list of some scholarships, and candidates may also visit the National Scholarship Portal. For scholarship-related assistance, write to nlsiuscholarship@nls.ac.in.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">24. Does financial aid cover the full fee?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Financial aid depends on the applicable policy and the assessment of the candidate's income and wealth information. The amount, if any, will be communicated by NLSIU. If granted after fee payment, reimbursement will be made up to the approved extent.</p>

  {# ════════════════════════════════════════ #}
  {# SECTION D — Documents                   #}
  {# ════════════════════════════════════════ #}
  <p class="faq-section-title">D. Documents and in-person verification</p>

  <p class="faq-q">25. Which original documents must I bring for registration?</p>
  {% if is_pg %}
  <p class="faq-a">You must bring the original Class 10 transcript, Class 12 transcript, Bachelor's degree certificate and transcript, and applicable caste, EWS, disability, and Karnataka category documents. You must also bring any other forms or documents sent by NLSIU before registration.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="faq-a">You must bring the original Class 10 transcript, Class 12 transcript, and applicable caste, EWS, disability, and Karnataka category documents. You must also bring any other forms or documents sent by NLSIU before registration.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="faq-q">26. What if my {% if is_pg %}Bachelor's degree certificate or final transcript{% else %}Class XII certificate or final transcript{% endif %} is not yet available?</p>
  {% if is_pg %}
  <p class="faq-a">Candidates who have not yet received their Bachelor's degree certificate or final transcript must submit a declaration stating that the certificate/transcript will be submitted on or before {{ bachelors_deadline }}. Admission will remain provisional until the final degree certificate and marks transcript showing that the candidate meets the eligibility criteria are submitted.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="faq-a">Candidates who have written their Class XII examination in 2026 and not yet received their Class XII marksheet/certificate shall submit a Declaration to the effect that the Class XII Marksheet/Certificate shall be submitted on or before December 31, 2026 and that admission will remain provisional until the submission of certificate and marksheet indicating that the candidate has met the eligibility criteria. Submission of digilocker print out will not be sufficient. They will have to submit the official certificate by December 31, 2026.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="faq-q">27. Will scanned copies be enough?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. Scans may be uploaded as instructed, but original documents must be produced during in-person verification on {{ registration_date }}. Your admission will be confirmed only after successful verification of the originals.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">28. What happens if I cannot produce a required original document?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Failure to submit or produce a valid required certificate at verification may result in withdrawal of the provisional offer of admission. If a document is unavailable for a genuine reason, contact nlsat.query@nls.ac.in immediately and do not wait until the registration date.</p>

  {# ════════════════════════════════════════ #}
  {# SECTION E — Category certificates       #}
  {# ════════════════════════════════════════ #}
  <p class="faq-section-title">E. Category certificates and reservations</p>

  <p class="faq-q">29. What is the validity requirement for an EWS certificate?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">An EWS certificate must be valid at the time of admission and must not be older than one year, unless a different validity condition is specified in the certificate.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">30. What is the validity requirement for an OBC-NCL certificate?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">If the OBC-NCL certificate mentions a validity period, it must be within that validity period. If no validity period is mentioned, the certificate must not be older than one year. Candidates seeking OBC reservation must ensure that they meet the applicable category requirements.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">31. Which authorities can issue valid OBC-NCL or EWS certificates?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">OBC-NCL and EWS certificates should be issued by a competent authority such as a District Magistrate, Additional Magistrate, Collector, Deputy Commissioner, Additional Deputy Commissioner, Deputy Collector, First Class Stipendiary Magistrate, Sub-Divisional Magistrate, Taluka Magistrate, Executive Magistrate, Extra Assistant Commissioner not below the rank of First Class Stipendiary Magistrate, Chief Presidency Magistrate, Additional Chief Presidency Magistrate, Presidency Magistrate, Revenue Officer not below the rank of Tehsildar, or Sub-Divisional Officer of the area where the candidate or the candidate's family resides.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">32. Can I use an Income and Caste Certificate instead of an EWS certificate?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. A valid EWS certificate is required for EWS category eligibility. An Income and Caste Certificate is not sufficient for claiming reservation.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">33. Can I rely on a State Government OBC certificate?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Candidates claiming OBC reservation must ensure that the category claimed falls within the central list or the Karnataka OBC list for the category claimed.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">34. What is the validity for an SC/ST certificate?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">SC/ST certificates generally do not have a validity period. However, the certificate must be genuine, issued by a competent authority, and valid for the category claimed.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">35. What if my EWS, OBC-NCL, caste, disability or Karnataka document is under process?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">You must produce the valid original certificate at the time of verification. A pending application or acknowledgement is not a substitute for the required certificate.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">36. What should PWD candidates submit?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">PWD candidates must submit the disability certificate in the format as per the The Rights of Persons with Disabilities (RPwD) Act, 2016 (Form V or Form VI) signed and stamped by a competent authority or a valid Unique Disability ID(UDID) card.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">37. What documents are required for the Karnataka Students category?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Study certificates from recognised and affiliated schools or educational institutions showing the required period of study in Karnataka are required.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">38. Is a domicile certificate enough for the Karnataka Students category?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. Domicile certificates are not accepted as a substitute for study certificates and other required documents.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">39. Can study certificates issued in Kannada be submitted?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. Study certificates issued in Kannada by recognised schools or educational institutions are acceptable.</p>

  {# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
  {# SECTION G — Housing (programme-specific)                    #}
  {# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}

  {% if is_pg %}
  {# ──── PG Housing FAQ (LLB / MPP) — Q40-Q48 ──── #}
  <p class="faq-section-title">G. University off-campus accommodation and housing</p>

  <p class="faq-q">40. Is housing guaranteed?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. All students of the {{ prog_display }} programme are eligible to apply for off-campus accommodation, but applying does not guarantee allotment. Allocation will be made only at the time of admission and will depend on availability at that stage.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">41. How do I apply for University residence?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">When accepting the offer in the admissions portal, you will be asked whether you wish to apply for off-campus accommodation. Select "Yes" if you want to apply. The off-campus housing fee will then be added to your fee invoice.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">42. Can I choose not to apply for University residence?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. Select "No" in the portal if you do not want to apply for University off-campus accommodation. You may then independently arrange private accommodation.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">43. If I select "Yes", when must I pay the housing fee?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">If you select "Yes", the full off-campus housing fee of Rs. {{ housing_fee }} will be included in your fee invoice and must be paid by {{ full_fee_deadline }} along with the balance fee.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">44. Where are the University's off-campus residences located?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">NLSIU has tied up with housing service providers in RR Nagar, including Olive Living and FF21. RR Nagar is close to Nagarbhavi and is in the vicinity of the University. Scheduled transportation is provided to the university.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">45. Will rooms be single or shared? Can I request for a single room?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Rooms in University off-campus residences are allotted on a double-sharing basis.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">46. Can a student who is not living in the off-campus residences opt for the university meal plan?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. Students who have not opted for the off-campus residences can opt for the university meal plan and utilise the mess facilities on the payment of a meal plan fees every trimester. You may contact the residence life team during registration to enroll in the meal plan.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">47. Can NLSIU help me find private housing?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. Students may independently explore private hostels, paying guest facilities, or rental housing around Nagarbhavi depending on their budget and convenience. We encourage students who do not have housing in Bengaluru, to come to Bengaluru early to identify suitable options.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">48. Can parents or family members stay in University accommodation during registration?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">The NLSAT offer does not provide accommodation for parents or family members. Candidates and families accompanying them should make their own arrangements.</p>

  {# ──── PG Registration FAQ — Q49-Q55 ──── #}
  <p class="faq-section-title">H. Registration, orientation and joining NLSIU</p>

  <p class="faq-q">49. When must I report to campus?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">You are required to be present at the NLSIU campus in Bengaluru from {{ registration_date }} onwards for registration and onboarding. Original document verification will be conducted on {{ registration_date }} during the allotted registration slot.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">50. Can someone else complete registration on my behalf?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. The candidate must be present in person for registration and original document verification.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">51. Are parents required to attend registration?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. Parents are not required during registration and will not be allowed into campus during orientation and classes.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">52. Can I join late after registration or orientation?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. Candidates are expected to be present from the registration and orientation dates. Classes and academic requirements will be in person. Attendance is compulsory.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">53. Will there be online classes as an alternative to in-person attendance?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. Students are expected to attend in-person classes and comply with the applicable academic and attendance regulations.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">54. What is the attendance requirement?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Students must comply with the attendance requirements under applicable NLSIU regulations. As a general rule at NLSIU, shortage of attendance may affect eligibility to appear for examinations and may have serious academic consequences.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">55. Can I defer my admission to the next academic year?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. The provisional offer is for the academic year {{ academic_yr }}. NLSIU does not have provisions for deferral of admission to a later academic year.</p>

  {% else %}
  {# ──── UG Housing FAQ (BA) — Q40-Q45 ──── #}
  <p class="faq-section-title">G. University accommodation and housing</p>

  <p class="faq-q">40. Is housing guaranteed?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. All students of the {{ prog_display }} programme are eligible to apply for accommodation, but applying does not guarantee allotment. Allocation will be made only at the time of admission and will depend on availability at that stage.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">41. How do I apply for University residence?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">When accepting the offer in the admissions portal, you will be asked whether you wish to apply for accommodation. Select "Yes" if you want to apply. The housing fee will then be added to your fee invoice.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">42. Can I choose not to apply for University residence?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. Select "No" in the portal if you do not want to apply for University accommodation. You may then independently arrange private accommodation.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">43. If I select "Yes", when must I pay the housing fee?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">If you select "Yes", the full housing fee of Rs. {{ housing_fee }} will be included in your fee invoice and must be paid by {{ full_fee_deadline }} along with the balance fee.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">44. Can NLSIU help me find private housing?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. Students may independently explore private hostels, paying guest facilities, or rental housing around Nagarbhavi depending on their budget and convenience. We encourage students who do not have housing in Bengaluru, to come to Bengaluru early to identify suitable options.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">45. Can parents or family members stay in University accommodation during registration?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">The NLSAT offer does not provide accommodation for parents or family members. Candidates and families accompanying them should make their own arrangements.</p>

  {# ──── UG Registration FAQ — Q46-Q52 ──── #}
  <p class="faq-section-title">H. Registration, orientation and joining NLSIU</p>

  <p class="faq-q">46. When must I report to campus?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">You are required to be present at the NLSIU campus in Bengaluru from {{ registration_date }} onwards for registration and onboarding. Original document verification will be conducted on {{ registration_date }} during the allotted registration slot.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">47. Can someone else complete registration on my behalf?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. The candidate must be present in person for registration and original document verification.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">48. Are parents required to attend registration?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Yes. At least one parent of the candidate is compulsorily required during registration. However, parents will not be allowed into campus during orientation and classes.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">49. Can I join late after registration or orientation?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. Candidates are expected to be present from the registration and orientation dates. Classes and academic requirements will be in person. Attendance is compulsory.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">50. Will there be online classes as an alternative to in-person attendance?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. Students are expected to attend in-person classes and comply with the applicable academic and attendance regulations.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">51. What is the attendance requirement?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">Students must comply with the attendance requirements under applicable NLSIU regulations. As a general rule at NLSIU, shortage of attendance may affect eligibility to appear for examinations and may have serious academic consequences.</p>

  <p class="faq-q">52. Can I defer my admission to the next academic year?</p>
  <p class="faq-a">No. The provisional offer is for the academic year {{ academic_yr }}. NLSIU does not have provisions for deferral of admission to a later academic year.</p>

  {% endif %}

  <p class="para" style="margin-top:16px;">For any issue not covered above, candidates should write to nlsat.query@nls.ac.in using the subject line "NLSAT Admission Query – [insert admit card number]".</p>

  <div class="pg-footer">
    A University for Legal Studies and Research sponsored by the Bar Council of India and established under Karnataka Act 22 of 1986
  </div>
</div>

</div>{# end .nlsat-offer #}

{%- set ctx = get_results_notification_context(doc) -%}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8"/>
<style>
    * { box-sizing: border-box; -moz-box-sizing: border-box; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
    @page {
        size: A4;
        margin: 15mm 18mm 15mm 18mm;
    }
    html, body { margin: 0 !important; padding: 0 !important; background: #fff !important; width: 100%; }
    body { font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #1a1a1a; line-height: 1.45; font-weight: normal; }

    .doc-wrap { width: 100%; max-width: 100%; margin: 0 auto; background: #fff; position: relative; }

    /* Header */
    .hdr-tbl { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 2px solid #222222; padding-bottom: 8px; }
    .hdr-tbl td { vertical-align: middle; }
    .logo-cell { width: 100px; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; padding-right: 12px; }
    .logo-img { max-width: 90px; max-height: 85px; object-fit: contain; }
    .univ-title { font-size: 19pt; font-weight: bold; color: #1a1a1a; text-transform: uppercase; font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 4px; letter-spacing: 0.01em; }
    .univ-address { font-size: 10.5pt; font-weight: 600; color: #333333; margin-top: 2px; font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; line-height: 1.35; }
    .univ-contact { font-size: 10pt; font-weight: 600; color: #333333; margin-top: 4px; font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; }

    /* Date */
    .date-row { text-align: right; font-size: 11pt; margin-bottom: 18px; font-weight: normal; color: #1a1a1a; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; }

    /* Document Heading */
    .doc-heading { text-align: center; font-size: 12.5pt; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; color: #1a1a1a; margin-bottom: 18px; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; line-height: 1.3; }

    /* Paragraphs */
    .para { font-size: 11pt; text-align: justify; color: #1a1a1a; margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.45; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-weight: normal; }

    /* Cutoff Table */
    .cutoff-tbl { width: 80%; margin: 14px auto 6px auto; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 10pt; page-break-inside: avoid; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #1a1a1a; }
    .cutoff-tbl th { border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 5px 8px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; background-color: #ffffff; color: #1a1a1a; font-size: 10pt; }
    .cutoff-tbl th.cat-hdr { text-align: left; }
    .cutoff-tbl td { border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 4px 8px; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; color: #1a1a1a; font-weight: normal; font-size: 10pt; }
    .cutoff-tbl td.cat-label { text-align: left; font-weight: 500; }
    .note-text { font-size: 9pt; text-align: left; margin: 4px 10% 16px 10%; color: #333333; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-style: italic; }

    /* Grid Tables for Admit Card Numbers */
    .grid-tbl { width: 100%; margin: 14px auto 16px auto; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 10pt; page-break-inside: auto; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #1a1a1a; }
    .grid-tbl tr { page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: auto; }
    .grid-tbl th { border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 4px 6px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; background: #ffffff; color: #1a1a1a; font-size: 10pt; }
    .grid-tbl td { border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 4px 6px; text-align: center; vertical-align: middle; color: #1a1a1a; font-weight: normal; font-size: 9.5pt; }
    .grid-tbl .sn-col { width: 10%; font-weight: 500; }
    .grid-tbl .ac-col { width: 23%; font-weight: 500; }

    /* Signature */
    .sig-section { margin-top: 30px; page-break-inside: avoid; }
    .sig-block { width: 180px; text-align: left; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; color: #1a1a1a; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; }

    /* Footer */
    .page-footer {
        margin-top: 30px;
        padding-top: 6px;
        border-top: 1px solid #1a1a1a;
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 8.5pt;
        color: #444444;
        font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;
    }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="doc-wrap">
    <!-- Header -->
    <table class="hdr-tbl">
        <tr>
            <td class="logo-cell">
                {% if ctx.logo_src %}
                    <img src="{{ ctx.logo_src }}" class="logo-img">
                {% else %}
                    <div style="width:90px; height:85px; border:1px solid #999; font-size:8pt; text-align:center; line-height:85px; font-weight:bold; color: #666;">LOGO</div>
                {% endif %}
            </td>
            <td style="text-align: left; padding-left: 10px; vertical-align: middle;">
                <div class="univ-title">{{ ctx.campus_name }}</div>
                {% if ctx.campus_address %}<div class="univ-address">{{ ctx.campus_address }}</div>{% endif %}
                {% if ctx.contact_info %}<div class="univ-contact">{{ ctx.contact_info }}</div>{% endif %}
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <!-- Date -->
    {% if ctx.date_str %}<div class="date-row">Date: {{ ctx.date_str }}</div>{% endif %}

    <!-- Title -->
    <div class="doc-heading"><u>{{ ctx.title }}</u></div>

    <!-- Paragraph 1 -->
    <div class="para">
        The {{ ctx.entrance_test_name }} was conducted for the admission process of {{ ctx.program_name }} at {{ ctx.campus_name }} for the Academic Year {{ ctx.academic_year }}. Candidates who attempted the {{ ctx.entrance_test_name }} examination may view their scorecards after logging into their profile on the {{ ctx.entrance_test_name }} admission portal ({{ ctx.portal_url }}).
    </div>

    <!-- Paragraph 2 -->
    <div class="para">
        The examination process involved independent evaluation and multiple stages of verification. Accordingly, requests for revaluation or review of scores shall not be entertained.
    </div>

    <!-- Paragraph 3 -->
    <div class="para">
        Based on the scores obtained in the examination, category-wise score cut-offs were determined in accordance with the notified admission process and applicable reservation policies. The category-wise cut-offs applied for provisional admission offers at this stage are provided in the table below:
    </div>

    <!-- Cut-off Table -->
    {% if ctx.cutoff_table %}
    <table class="cutoff-tbl">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th class="cat-hdr" style="width: 48%;">Category</th>
                <th style="width: 26%;">All India</th>
                <th style="width: 26%;">Karnataka (25% HC)</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for r in ctx.cutoff_table %}
            <tr>
                <td class="cat-label">{{ r.category }}</td>
                {% if r.is_span %}
                    <td colspan="2">{{ r.all_india }}</td>
                {% else %}
                    <td>{{ r.all_india }}</td>
                    <td>{{ r.karnataka }}</td>
                {% endif %}
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <div class="note-text">Note: H stands for Horizontal Reservation. HC stands for Horizontal Compartmentalised Reservation.</div>
    {% endif %}

    <!-- Paragraph 4 -->
    <div class="para">
        Candidates who met the minimum qualifying requirements and secured marks within the relevant cut-off for their seat category have been considered for provisional admission, subject to verification of documents, eligibility, payment of fees, and fulfilment of all other conditions prescribed by the University. The students with the following admit card numbers have been provisionally offered admission to the programme:
    </div>

    <!-- Provisionally Selected Grid Table -->
    {% if ctx.selected_grid_rows %}
    <table class="grid-tbl">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th class="sn-col"><u>S.No</u></th>
                <th class="ac-col">Admit Card Number</th>
                <th class="sn-col"><u>S.No</u></th>
                <th class="ac-col">Admit Card Number</th>
                <th class="sn-col"><u>S.No</u></th>
                <th class="ac-col">Admit Card Number</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for r in ctx.selected_grid_rows %}
            <tr>
                <td class="sn-col">{{ r.col1.s_no if r.col1 else '' }}</td>
                <td class="ac-col">{{ r.col1.admit_card_number if r.col1 else '' }}</td>
                <td class="sn-col">{{ r.col2.s_no if r.col2 else '' }}</td>
                <td class="ac-col">{{ r.col2.admit_card_number if r.col2 else '' }}</td>
                <td class="sn-col">{{ r.col3.s_no if r.col3 else '' }}</td>
                <td class="ac-col">{{ r.col3.admit_card_number if r.col3 else '' }}</td>
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    {% else %}
    <div style="padding: 10px; text-align: center; color: #666; font-style: italic;">No provisionally selected candidates found.</div>
    {% endif %}

    <!-- Waitlist Section -->
    <div class="para" style="margin-top: 15px;">
        Based on the scores obtained in the examination, the students with the following admit card numbers have been placed on a waiting list:
    </div>

    <!-- Waitlist Grid Table -->
    {% if ctx.waitlist_grid_rows %}
    <table class="grid-tbl">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th class="sn-col"><u>S.No</u></th>
                <th class="ac-col">Admit Card Number</th>
                <th class="sn-col"><u>S.No</u></th>
                <th class="ac-col">Admit Card Number</th>
                <th class="sn-col"><u>S.No</u></th>
                <th class="ac-col">Admit Card Number</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for r in ctx.waitlist_grid_rows %}
            <tr>
                <td class="sn-col">{{ r.col1.s_no if r.col1 else '' }}</td>
                <td class="ac-col">{{ r.col1.admit_card_number if r.col1 else '' }}</td>
                <td class="sn-col">{{ r.col2.s_no if r.col2 else '' }}</td>
                <td class="ac-col">{{ r.col2.admit_card_number if r.col2 else '' }}</td>
                <td class="sn-col">{{ r.col3.s_no if r.col3 else '' }}</td>
                <td class="ac-col">{{ r.col3.admit_card_number if r.col3 else '' }}</td>
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    {% else %}
    <div style="padding: 10px; text-align: center; color: #666; font-style: italic;">No waitlisted candidates.</div>
    {% endif %}

    <!-- Closing Paragraph -->
    <div class="para" style="margin-top: 15px;">
        Students on the waiting list will be offered admission, in order of their ranks, whenever a candidate who is provisionally offered admission declines the offer, fails to pay the requisite fees or withdraws from the admission process.
    </div>

    <!-- Signature Block -->
    <div class="sig-section">
        <div class="sig-block">
            <div style="margin-bottom: 35px;"></div>
            <div>{{ ctx.signatory }}</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <div class="page-footer">
        A University for Legal Studies and Research sponsored by the Bar Council of India and established under Karnataka Act 22 of 1986
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>

{% set ctx = get_transcript_context(doc.student) %}
{% set t = ctx.template %}
{% set s = ctx.student %}
{% set years = ctx.years %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"/>
<style>
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body { font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; color: #111; background: #fff; }
  .page-wrap { width: 100%; padding: 12px 14px; border: 1.5px solid #d8c8c2; box-sizing: border-box; }

  /* Header */
  .hdr { background: #c84630; padding: 10px 14px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 22px; }
  .hdr-logo img { object-fit: contain; }
  .hdr-text { flex: 1; }
  .hdr-inst-name { font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }
  .hdr-subtitle  { font-size: 8.5pt; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); margin-top: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.8px; }
  .hdr-address   { font-size: 7.5pt; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75); margin-top: 2px; }

  /* Student Info row */
  .student-row { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; padding: 8px 14px 6px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0; }
  .student-photo { width: 50px; height: 60px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 2px; border: 1px solid #ddd; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 18px; }
  .student-photo-placeholder { width: 50px; height: 60px; background: #e8eaed; border-radius: 2px; flex-shrink: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 7pt; color: #aaa; margin-right: 18px; }
  .student-info { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
  .student-name { font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; color: #111; }
  .student-meta { font-size: 8.5pt; color: #555; margin-top: 2px; }
  .cgpa-box { text-align: right; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .cgpa-label { font-size: 7.5pt; color: #888; }
  .cgpa-value { font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; color: #c84630; line-height: 1.1; }

  /* Watermark */
  .watermark-wrap { position: relative; }
  .watermark { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(-30deg);
               pointer-events: none; z-index: 0; white-space: nowrap;
               font-size: 42pt; font-weight: 900; color: #c84630; letter-spacing: 4px; }
  .watermark-img { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
                   pointer-events: none; z-index: 0; max-width: 55%; max-height: 55%; }
  .content-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; }

  /* Semester section */
  .semester-section { padding: 6px 14px 0; }
  .sem-header { font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: bold; color: #c84630; margin-bottom: 3px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }

  /* Course table */
  .course-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .course-table th { background: #fce8e6; padding: 3px 6px; text-align: left; font-size: 8.5pt; border: 1px solid #e0c8c4; font-weight: 600; }
  .course-table th.center, .course-table td.center { text-align: center; }
  .course-table td { padding: 3px 6px; font-size: 9pt; border: 1px solid #eee; vertical-align: middle; }
  .course-table tr:nth-child(even) td { background: #fafafa; }
  .course-table tr:nth-child(odd) td { background: #fff; }
  .grade-failed { color: #c00; }
  .mfa-sup { color: #d97706; font-weight: 700; font-size: 70%; }

  /* SGPA row */
  .sgpa-row { text-align: right; font-size: 8pt; color: #555; padding: 2px 0 4px; }
  .sgpa-row span { font-weight: bold; color: #333; }

  /* Footer / signatures */
  .footer { margin-top: 14px; padding: 8px 14px 10px; border-top: 1px solid #e0e0e0; }
  .cgpa-line { font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 8px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }
  .sig-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-around; align-items: flex-end; margin-top: 10px; }
  .sig-block { text-align: center; }
  .sig-block img { max-height: 28px; display: block; margin: 0 auto 2px; }
  .sig-line { width: 90px; border-bottom: 1px solid #888; margin: 0 auto 2px; }
  .sig-label { font-size: 8pt; color: #333; }
  .date-line { font-size: 8pt; color: #666; text-align: center; margin-top: 6px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page-wrap">

  <!-- Header -->
  <div class="hdr">
    {% if t.show_institute_logo and t.institute_logo %}
    <div class="hdr-logo" style="text-align: {{ (t.logo_alignment or 'center') | lower }};">
      <img src="{{ t.institute_logo }}" style="max-height: {{ [30, [60, (t.logo_width or 120) * 0.45 | int] | min] | max }}px; max-width: {{ t.logo_width or 120 }}px;"/>
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <div style="width: 42px; height: 42px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.22); border-radius: 50%; flex-shrink: 0;"></div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="hdr-text">
      <div class="hdr-inst-name">{{ t.institute_name or 'Institute Name' }}</div>
      <div class="hdr-subtitle">{{ t.header_title or 'OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT OF ACADEMIC RECORDS' }}</div>
      {% if t.show_institute_address and t.institute_address_full %}
      <div class="hdr-address">{{ t.institute_address_full }}</div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Student Info Row -->
  <div class="student-row">
    {% if t.show_student_photo %}
      {% if s.passport_size_photo %}
      <img class="student-photo" src="{{ s.passport_size_photo }}" alt="Photo"/>
      {% else %}
      <div class="student-photo-placeholder">Photo</div>
      {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
    <div class="student-info">
      <div class="student-name">{{ s.full_name }}</div>
      {% if t.show_registration_id and (s.registration_id or doc.student) %}
      <div class="student-meta">Student ID: {{ s.registration_id or doc.student }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if s.programme_name %}
      <div class="student-meta">Programme: {{ s.programme_name }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if s.batch_year %}
      <div class="student-meta">Batch: {{ s.batch_year }}</div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% if t.show_cgpa and ctx.cgpa %}
    <div class="cgpa-box">
      <div class="cgpa-label">CGPA</div>
      <div class="cgpa-value">{{ ctx.cgpa }}</div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <!-- Watermark + Content -->
  {% set show_wm = t.show_watermark and (t.watermark_logo or t.watermark_text) %}
  <div class="{% if show_wm %}watermark-wrap{% endif %}">
    {% if show_wm %}
      {% set wm_op = ((t.watermark_opacity or 20) | int) / 100 %}
      {% if t.watermark_logo %}
      <img class="watermark-img" src="{{ t.watermark_logo }}" style="opacity: {{ wm_op }};" />
      {% else %}
      <div class="watermark" style="opacity: {{ wm_op }};">{{ t.watermark_text }}</div>
      {% endif %}
    {% endif %}

    <div class="content-inner">

      {% if years %}
        {% for year in years %}
        <div class="semester-section">
          {% if t.show_semester_wise %}
          <div class="sem-header">{{ year.label }}</div>
          {% endif %}

          <table class="course-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="center" style="width: 15%;">Course<br>No.</th>
                <th>Prescribed Courses</th>
                <th class="center" style="width: 20%;">Grade<br>Obtained</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {% for c in year.courses %}
              <tr>
                <td class="center">{{ c.course_number }}</td>
                <td>{{ c.course_name }}</td>
                <td class="center {% if c.is_failed %}grade-failed{% endif %}">{{ c.grade_html | safe }}</td>
              </tr>
              {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>

        </div>
        {% endfor %}

      {% else %}
      <div style="padding: 20px 14px; text-align: center; color: #888; font-size: 9pt;">
        No course records found for this student.
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      <!-- Footer -->
      <div class="footer">
        {% if t.show_cgpa and ctx.cgpa %}
        <div class="cgpa-line">
          Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA): {{ ctx.cgpa }}
        </div>
        {% endif %}

        <!-- Signatures -->
        {% set has_sig = (t.sig_label_1 or t.sig_image_1) or (t.sig_label_2 or t.sig_image_2) or (t.sig_label_3 or t.sig_image_3) %}
        {% if has_sig %}
        <div class="sig-row">
          {% for n in [1, 2, 3] %}
            {% set lbl = t['sig_label_' ~ n] %}
            {% set img = t['sig_image_' ~ n] %}
            {% if lbl or img %}
            <div class="sig-block">
              {% if img %}
              <img src="{{ img }}" style="max-height: 28px;"/>
              {% else %}
              <div class="sig-line"></div>
              {% endif %}
              {% if lbl %}<div class="sig-label">{{ lbl }}</div>{% endif %}
            </div>
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="date-line">Date: {{ ctx.generation_date }}</div>
      </div>

    </div><!-- .content-inner -->
  </div><!-- .watermark-wrap -->

</div><!-- .page-wrap -->
</body>
</html>
